{"id": "rivian-2026-11-14-010", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": ["rivian"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "I finally got a USB-C charging e-bike, and it costs 75% less than Rivian’s bike", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/05/engwe-zip-foldig-bike-head.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I’ve been <a href=\"https://electrek.co/2022/06/23/electric-bike-usb-c-battery-chargers/\">waiting years</a> for electric bikes to finally embrace USB-C charging. We’ve already standardized much of our lives around the convenient little connector, from phones and laptops to tablets and countless other ga", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/14/i-finally-got-a-usb-c-charging-e-bike-and-it-costs-75-less-than-rivians-bike/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "tesla-2026-11-14-011", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": ["tesla"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Tesla Cybercab orders open at $29,990 + $299/mo, only in Robotaxi zones", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/11/Tesla-Cybercab-orders.jpeg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Tesla is now inviting “select customers” to buy a Cybercab for personal use at $29,990, but the car won’t move unless you also pay $299 a month for an “Autonomy Subscription.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And it only works inside Tesla’s Robotaxi service areas in Texas and Florida, the same geofenc", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/13/tesla-cybercab-personal-use-orders-299-subscription-geofence/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "tesla-2026-11-14-012", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": ["tesla"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Tesla Opens Self-Driving Cybercab Orders To 'Select Customers' At $29,990", "content": "The Cybercab will be Tesla's cheapest vehicle, but there's a catch: autonomous driving will cost you $299 per month. ", "sources": [{"name": "insideevs", "url": "https://insideevs.com/news/815473/tesla-cybercab-pricing-sales-announced/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "tesla-2026-11-14-013", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": ["tesla"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Tesla Starts Selling Cybercab — $30,000*", "content": "<p>Well, it&#8217;s a big day in Tesla World. The company has officially launched Cybercab sales. You can now order a Cybercab for the starting price of $30,000 (technically, $29,900). That said, there is an asterisk here — actually, there are two asterisks here. First of all, only people who have   ... [continued]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://cleantechnica.com/2026/11/13/tesla-starts-selling-cybercab-30000/\">Tesla Starts Selling Cybercab — $30,000*</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cle", "sources": [{"name": "cleantechnica", "url": "https://cleantechnica.com/2026/11/13/tesla-starts-selling-cybercab-30000/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-014", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Who Can Weather the Health Storm?", "content": "<p>States facing the greatest health damage from climate change are the least equipped to protect their residents. Across the United States, climate change is intensifying extreme weather events, resulting in escalating public health harms and severe economic damage. For example, devastating inland flooding in Texas in 2025 killed 134 people   ... [continued]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://cleantechnica.com/2026/11/13/who-can-weather-the-health-storm/\">Who Can Weather the Health Storm?</a> app", "sources": [{"name": "cleantechnica", "url": "https://cleantechnica.com/2026/11/13/who-can-weather-the-health-storm/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-015", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "First attempt to address screen printing-induced degradation in copper-plated heterojunction solar cells", "content": "<p>Researchers in China have investigated a previously overlooked degradation mechanism in copper-plated heterojunction solar cells caused by screen-printed photoresist. They found that progressive wear of the screen mesh can damage the cells' passivation layers and reduce efficiency. An optimized emulsion buffer layer reportedly prevented the degradation over 40,000 consecutive printing cycles.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/first-attempt-to-address-screen-print", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/first-attempt-to-address-screen-printing-induced-degradation-in-copper-plated-heterojunction-solar-cells/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-016", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "UNSW develops three-minute lithium-ion battery health test", "content": "<p>Researchers at the University of New South Wales (UNSW) have developed a prototype that uses electrical pulses and statistical models to assess lithium-ion battery health in under three minutes per cell, with a potential role in sorting retired batteries for reuse or recycling. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/unsw-develops-three-minute-lithium-ion-battery-health-test/\">UNSW develops three-minute lithium-ion battery health test</a> appeared first on <a href=\"ht", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/unsw-develops-three-minute-lithium-ion-battery-health-test/", "type": "rss"}]}
